1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,680
Mark 9

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:04,400
And he said to them,

3
00:00:05,060 --> 00:00:13,920
Truly I say to you, there are some standing here who will not taste death until they see the kingdom of God, after it has come with power.

4
00:00:14,420 --> 00:00:21,360
And after six days Jesus took with him Peter and James and John, and led them up a high mountain by themselves.

5
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:28,980
And he was transfigured before them, and his clothes became radiant, intensely white, as no one on earth could bleach them.

6
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:33,700
And there appeared to them Elijah with Moses, and they were talking with Jesus.

7
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,820
And Peter said to Jesus,

8
00:00:36,780 --> 00:00:44,520
Rabbi, it is good that we are here. Let us make three tents, one for you, and one for Moses, and one for Elijah.

9
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:48,300
For he did not know what to say, for they were terrified.

10
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:52,360
And a cloud overshadowed them, and a voice came out of the cloud,

11
00:00:52,980 --> 00:00:56,700
This is my beloved son. Listen to him.

12
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:58,960
And suddenly, looking around,

13
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:02,240
they no longer saw anyone with them but Jesus only.

14
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:07,660
And as they were coming down the mountain, he charged them to tell no one what they had seen,

15
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:10,540
until the Son of Man had risen from the dead.

16
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:16,780
So they kept the matter to themselves, questioning what this rising from the dead might mean.

17
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,020
And they asked him,

18
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:21,460
Why do the scribes say that first Elijah must come?

19
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:23,220
And he said to them,

20
00:01:23,900 --> 00:01:26,720
Elijah does come first, to restore all things.

21
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:28,960
And how is it written of the Son of Man,

22
00:01:29,080 --> 00:01:32,520
that he should suffer many things, and be treated with contempt?

23
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:35,520
But I tell you that Elijah has come,

24
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:39,740
and they did to him whatever they pleased, as it is written of him.

25
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,340
And when they came to the disciples,

26
00:01:43,580 --> 00:01:46,840
they saw a great crowd around them, and scribes arguing with them.

27
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:49,900
And immediately all the crowd, when they saw him,

28
00:01:50,140 --> 00:01:53,160
were greatly amazed, and ran up to him, and greeted him.

29
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:54,500
And he asked them,

30
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,120
What are you arguing about with them?

31
00:01:57,880 --> 00:01:58,960
And someone from the crowd,

32
00:01:59,080 --> 00:02:00,280
answered him,

33
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:05,180
Teacher, I brought my son to you, for he has a spirit that makes him mute,

34
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:08,080
and whenever it seizes him, it throws him down,

35
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:11,180
and he foams and grinds his teeth, and becomes rigid.

36
00:02:11,580 --> 00:02:15,280
So I asked your disciples that cast it out, and they were not able.

37
00:02:15,980 --> 00:02:17,180
And he answered them,

38
00:02:17,780 --> 00:02:21,880
O faithless generation, how long am I to be with you?

39
00:02:22,180 --> 00:02:24,480
How long am I to bear with you?

40
00:02:25,380 --> 00:02:26,380
Bring him to me.

41
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,480
And they brought the boy to him.

42
00:02:28,980 --> 00:02:32,380
And when the spirit saw him, immediately it convulsed the boy,

43
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:35,760
and he fell on the ground, and rolled about, foaming at the mouth.

44
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:37,640
And Jesus asked his father,

45
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:40,700
How long has this been happening to him?

46
00:02:41,380 --> 00:02:42,160
And he said,

47
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:43,840
From childhood.

48
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:48,980
And it is often cast him into fire, and into water, to destroy him.

49
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:53,680
But if you can do anything, have compassion on us, and help us.

50
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,740
And Jesus said to him,

51
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:57,440
If you can,

52
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:00,600
then all things are possible for one who believes.

53
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:04,540
Immediately the father of the child cried out and said,

54
00:03:05,040 --> 00:03:06,080
I believe.

55
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:08,640
Help my unbelief.

56
00:03:09,360 --> 00:03:12,120
And when Jesus saw that a crowd came running together,

57
00:03:12,380 --> 00:03:14,940
he rebuked the unclean spirit, saying to it,

58
00:03:15,780 --> 00:03:20,840
You mute and deaf spirit, I command you, come out of him, and never enter him again.

59
00:03:21,540 --> 00:03:24,280
And after crying out and convulsing him terribly,

60
00:03:24,280 --> 00:03:27,000
it came out, and the boy was like a corpse.

61
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,780
So that most of them said,

62
00:03:29,560 --> 00:03:30,920
He is dead.

63
00:03:31,700 --> 00:03:35,460
But Jesus took him by the hand, and lifted him up, and he arose.

64
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:39,640
And when he had entered the house, his disciples asked him privately,

65
00:03:40,340 --> 00:03:41,900
Why could we not cast it out?

66
00:03:42,620 --> 00:03:43,840
And he said to them,

67
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:47,940
This kind cannot be driven out by anything but prayer.

68
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:52,380
They went on from there, and passed through Galilee.

69
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:56,760
And he did not want anyone to know, for he was teaching his disciples,

70
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:57,340
saying,

71
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:01,500
The Son of Man is going to be delivered into the hands of men,

72
00:04:01,860 --> 00:04:02,940
and they will kill him.

73
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:07,440
And when he is killed, after three days he will rise.

74
00:04:07,860 --> 00:04:11,760
But they did not understand the saying, and were afraid to ask him.

75
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:17,880
And they came to Capernaum, and when he was in the house, he asked them,

76
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,280
What were you discussing on the way?

77
00:04:20,960 --> 00:04:26,020
But they kept silent, for on the way they had argued with one another about who was the greatest.

78
00:04:26,560 --> 00:04:27,360
And he sat down, and said,

79
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:28,460
And he sat down, and called the twelve.

80
00:04:28,820 --> 00:04:29,800
And he said to them,

81
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:35,320
If anyone would be first, he must be last of all, and servant of all.

82
00:04:36,020 --> 00:04:38,400
And he took a child, and put him in the midst of them.

83
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:40,780
And taking him in his arms, he said to them,

84
00:04:41,500 --> 00:04:45,120
Whoever receives one such child in my name receives me.

85
00:04:45,780 --> 00:04:49,920
And whoever receives me receives not me, but him who sent me.

86
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,640
John said to him,

87
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:55,580
Teacher, we saw someone casting out demons in your name,

88
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:56,940
and we tried to stop him,

89
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,580
but he was not following us.

90
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,240
But Jesus said,

91
00:05:00,980 --> 00:05:02,360
Do not stop him,

92
00:05:02,700 --> 00:05:05,160
for no one who does a mighty work in my name

93
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:07,820
will be able soon afterward to speak evil of me.

94
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,540
For the one who is not against us is for us.

95
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,120
For truly I say to you,

96
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:17,720
whoever gives you a cup of water to drink because you belong to Christ

97
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:20,260
will by no means lose his reward.

98
00:05:21,520 --> 00:05:25,460
Whoever causes one of these little ones who believe in me to sin,

99
00:05:25,460 --> 00:05:27,120
it would be better for him,

100
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:29,500
if a great millstone were hung around his neck,

101
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,240
and he were thrown into the sea.

102
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,500
And if your hand causes you to sin,

103
00:05:34,900 --> 00:05:35,700
cut it off.

104
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,640
It is better for you to enter life crippled

105
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:40,720
than with two hands to go to hell,

106
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:42,440
to the unquenchable fire.

107
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:45,000
And if your foot causes you to sin,

108
00:05:45,140 --> 00:05:45,760
cut it off.

109
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,280
It is better for you to enter life lame

110
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:50,780
than with two feet to be thrown into hell.

111
00:05:51,760 --> 00:05:54,320
And if your eye causes you to sin,

112
00:05:54,740 --> 00:05:55,540
tear it out.

113
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:56,960
It is better for you to enter life lame,

114
00:05:56,960 --> 00:05:58,920
than to enter the kingdom of God with one eye,

115
00:05:59,260 --> 00:06:01,440
than with two eyes to be thrown into hell,

116
00:06:01,980 --> 00:06:03,940
where their worm does not die,

117
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,800
and the fire is not quenched.

118
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:08,680
For everyone will be salted with fire.

119
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:10,560
Salt is good,

120
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:12,740
but if the salt is lost its saltiness,

121
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,020
how will you make it salty again?

122
00:06:16,140 --> 00:06:17,780
Have salt in yourselves,

123
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:20,260
and be at peace with one another.

